p.src:
There is a second piece of arithmetic here, and it explains why wholesaling feels powerful. A relatively small amount of cash controls a much larger contractual position. If we define $L_{\mathrm{control}}=
\frac{V_{\mathrm{contract}}}{E_{\mathrm{earnest+option}}},$ then the spoken numbers give $L_{\mathrm{control}}
\approx
\frac{2{,}000{,}000}{20{,}000}
=100.$ This is best understood as contract-control leverage: a small committed amount secures rights over a much larger transaction path.

